{"id":"roc-auc","title":"ROC AUC with Tied Scores","difficulty":"Hard","pattern":"ML Coding","tags":["Metrics","Ranking","Sorting","Statistics"],"companies":{"apple":4,"google":3,"meta":3,"amazon":3,"microsoft":2},"description":"Compute the **area under the ROC curve** from a list of real-valued `scores` and a list of binary `labels` (1 = positive, 0 = negative).\n\nAUC equals the probability that a randomly chosen positive is scored higher than a randomly chosen negative, with **ties counting one half**. Implement it with the rank-based (Mann-Whitney U) formulation: assign each score its 1-based rank in ascending order, giving **tied scores the average of the ranks they span**, then\n\n`AUC = (sum of positive ranks - P * (P + 1) / 2) / (P * N)`\n\nwhere `P` and `N` are the numbers of positives and negatives. If either class is absent the metric is undefined; return `0.5` in that case. Aim for O(n log n).","examples":[{"input":"scores = [0.1, 0.4, 0.35, 0.8], labels = [0, 0, 1, 1]","output":"0.75","explanation":"Ranks are 0.1->1, 0.35->2, 0.4->3, 0.8->4. Positive ranks sum to 2 + 4 = 6; (6 - 3) / (2 * 2) = 0.75. Equivalently 3 of the 4 positive/negative pairs are ordered correctly."},{"input":"scores = [0.3, 0.3, 0.6], labels = [0, 1, 1]","output":"0.75","explanation":"The two 0.3 scores share rank 1.5. Pairs: (0.3 pos vs 0.3 neg) counts 0.5, (0.6 vs 0.3) counts 1; the mean is 0.75."},{"input":"scores = [0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5], labels = [0, 1, 0, 1]","output":"0.5","explanation":"A constant scorer orders nothing, which is exactly chance level."}],"constraints":["1 <= len(scores) == len(labels) <= 10^5","labels[i] in {0, 1}","Compared with tolerance 1e-5."],"hints":["The O(P * N) pairwise definition is a fine first answer, but the interviewer wants O(n log n).","Sort indices by score. Walk the sorted list in groups of equal scores; every member of a group gets the average rank of the group.","The sum of positive ranks over-counts the P*(P+1)/2 positive-positive comparisons; subtracting them leaves the number of (positive beats negative) pairs, ties counted as 0.5."],"function":"rocAuc","signature":"def rocAuc(self, scores: List[float], labels: List[int]) -> float:","arg_types":{"scores":"List[float]","labels":"List[int]"},"return_type":"float","compare":"float","tests":[{"input":{"scores":[0.1,0.4,0.35,0.8],"labels":[0,0,1,1]},"output":0.75},{"input":{"scores":[0.3,0.3,0.6],"labels":[0,1,1]},"output":0.75},{"input":{"scores":[0.5,0.5,0.5,0.5],"labels":[0,1,0,1]},"output":0.5},{"input":{"scores":[0.2,0.9,0.1,0.8],"labels":[0,1,0,1]},"output":1.0},{"input":{"scores":[0.9,0.1,0.8,0.2],"labels":[0,1,0,1]},"output":0.0},{"input":{"scores":[0.7,0.2],"labels":[1,1]},"output":0.5},{"input":{"scores":[0.2,0.5,0.5,0.5,0.9,0.1,0.5],"labels":[0,1,0,1,1,0,0]},"output":0.833333},{"input":{"scores":[0.0,0.37,0.74,0.1,0.47,0.84,0.2,0.57,0.94,0.3,0.67,0.03,0.4,0.77,0.13,0.5,0.87,0.23,0.6,0.97,0.33,0.7,0.06,0.43,0.8,0.16,0.53,0.9,0.26,0.63,1.0,0.36,0.73,0.09,0.46,0.83,0.19,0.56,0.93,0.29,0.66,0.02,0.39,0.76,0.12,0.49,0.86,0.22,0.59,0.96,0.32,0.69,0.05,0.42,0.79,0.15,0.52,0.89,0.25,0.62,0.99,0.35,0.72,0.08,0.45,0.82,0.18,0.55,0.92,0.28,0.65,0.01,0.38,0.75,0.11,0.48,0.85,0.21,0.58,0.95,0.31,0.68,0.04,0.41,0.78,0.14,0.51,0.88,0.24,0.61,0.98,0.34,0.71,0.07,0.44,0.81,0.17,0.54,0.91,0.27,0.64,0.0,0.37,0.74,0.1,0.47,0.84,0.2,0.57,0.94,0.3,0.67,0.03,0.4,0.77,0.13,0.5,0.87,0.23,0.6,0.97,0.33,0.7,0.06,0.43,0.8,0.16,0.53,0.9,0.26,0.63,1.0,0.36,0.73,0.09,0.46,0.83,0.19,0.56,0.93,0.29,0.66,0.02,0.39,0.76,0.12,0.49,0.86,0.22,0.59,0.96,0.32,0.69,0.05,0.42,0.79,0.15,0.52,0.89,0.25,0.62,0.99,0.35,0.72,0.08,0.45,0.82,0.18,0.55,0.92,0.28,0.65,0.01,0.38,0.75,0.11,0.48,0.85,0.21,0.58,0.95,0.31,0.68,0.04,0.41,0.78,0.14,0.51,0.88,0.24,0.61,0.98,0.34,0.71,0.07,0.44,0.81,0.17,0.54,0.91,0.27,0.64,0.0,0.37,0.74,0.1,0.47,0.84,0.2,0.57,0.94,0.3,0.67,0.03,0.4,0.77,0.13,0.5,0.87,0.23,0.6,0.97,0.33,0.7,0.06,0.43,0.8,0.16,0.53,0.9,0.26,0.63,1.0,0.36,0.73,0.09,0.46,0.83,0.19,0.56,0