 by sorted position alone (no averaging) makes the result depend on the sort's stability and over- or under-counts tied pairs. Group equal scores and give every member `(first_rank + last_rank) / 2`. Compare scores for equality after sorting, not via float arithmetic on differences.\n\n**Interview follow-ups:** How does this relate to the ROC curve? (sweeping the threshold traces TPR vs FPR; the trapezoidal area is the same number). Why can AUC look fine under heavy class imbalance while the model is useless, and why prefer PR-AUC then? (FPR stays tiny when negatives dominate; precision does not). How would you compute it in a streaming or distributed setting? (histogram the scores into bins, accept approximation). What does AUC = 0 tell you? (perfectly inverted scores).","complexity":{"time":"O(n log n)","space":"O(n)"},"similar":["precision-recall-f1","ndcg-at-k"],"number":211,"starter":"class Solution:\n    def rocAuc(self, scores: List[float], labels: List[int]) -> float:\n        pass\n"}